# App Experts for Building

When the user asks to **build**, **develop**, **add**, or **extend** features for Cyprus Winter, use the App Experts team.

## How to invoke

Use `mcp_task` with `subagent_type: "TEAM-AGENTS"` and specify the expert in the prompt. Always reference `.cursor/skills/cyprus-tourism-app/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/TEAM_APP_EXPERTS.md`.

## Lead expert by task

| Task | Lead | Support |
|------|------|---------|
| Add attraction/winery/trail | content-polish | senior-software-engineer, branding-redesign |
| Add new page | senior-software-engineer | branding-redesign, content-polish |
| New API route | senior-software-engineer | shell |
| Improve conversion funnel | ux-polish | content-polish |
| Refactor components | senior-software-engineer | branding-redesign |
| Content audit | content-polish | audit-explore |
| Pre-launch checklist | audit-explore | All |

## Example

```javascript
mcp_task({
  subagent_type: "TEAM-AGENTS",
  description: "Add new attraction page",
  prompt: "You are the architecture expert for Cyprus Winter. Reference .cursor/skills/cyprus-tourism-app/SKILL.md and .cursor/TEAM_APP_EXPERTS.md. Task: [user's task]. Use src/data/ as source of truth, follow existing patterns (PlanItem, getPlaceById), preserve type safety."
})
```

## Fallback

If `mcp_task` or TEAM-AGENTS is unavailable, simulate App Experts: consider Architecture, UX, Design, Content, and Audit concerns; reference the skill file; implement accordingly.
